			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-299869">
									

<p>You may be able to pick it up on a metal detector, but i think with it being made of carbon and such, it would probably not register in any serous way. Now, if some parts had already been replaced with metal components, then it would be very easy.</p>
<p>That is true…but then, sick animals typically withdraw and hide while they try to recover. Plus, there's no guarantee that a subject will survive the process, and while they are changing, they are very weak due to the pain and all the alterations, and make easy prey. The full gestation can take a while as well, so unless it's a very fast-acting strain, a insect may die before it shows any symptoms.</p>
<p>No problem, i like answering questions!</p>

